  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Self-check",
      "items": [
        "There is no minimum wave width or occupancy: a narrow or fully serialized graph is valid when every edge names an admissible serialization reason",
        "Ready independent nodes use available slots; excess work queues without artificial edges, and no work is invented to fill slots",
        "Width never triggers a rebuild; only an edge without an admissible reason is removed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rules",
      "items": [
        "Exclusive writable sets, frozen contracts before dispatch, no checks on staged work",
        "One integration gate per slice: full build, lint and tests run only in one Verify unit on the materialized workspace after its writers finish",
        "A milestone commit is a separate decision after acceptance passes; non-blocking advisory findings stay recorded and do not block",
        "Integrating starts once phase verdicts pass consolidated; recovery follows a second failure or contract defect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Slice control",
      "items": [
        "Once a slice is accepted, evaluate it before the next slice and tell a participating user how to try it",
        "Dropping, adding or refactoring work alters the story first and realigns the invariants derived from it",
        "A narrow or fully serialized slice remains valid; only an incomplete or unbounded contract returns to its author"
      ]
    }
  ]
